\title{Weeknotes for 15 May 2026 (week 19)}
\author{brentyorgey}
\date{2026-05-16}
\tag{weeknote}

\put\transclude/numbered{false}

\subtree{
  \title{Still still wrapping up the semester...}

  \p{This week was even worse than last week: students turning in last-minute assignments at the start of the week, submitting final course grades, dealing with lots of academic integrity (aka cheating) cases (I am the chair of my college's academic integrity committee), conducting a last-minute search for a one-year visiting position (I'm the chair of my department and hence the \em{de facto} chair of the search committee), participating in a half-day workshop for a new first-year course I will be teaching in the fall... and on top of all that, my church has hired a new pastor who will be arriving soon, and there has been a lot of work getting ready for his arrival and organizing his ordination service.  Basically, I find myself in several leadership positions, all of which required more work than usual over the past few weeks in particular!  I definitely didn't have time to write the blog post I promised last week. Fortunately, in all cases there is light at the end of the tunnel: academic integrity stuff is finished; the search is proceeding well after the initial flurry of reading lots of applications; and almost everything is arranged for our new pastor's arrival.  I always hesitate to say "next week will be better", because I am frequently wrong.  But I really do think next week I will be able to start easing into some summer projects.}
}
